libFLAC
-------

The FLAC decoder of each implementation of WFDB-x is a translation of the
stream decoder of libFLAC 1.4.3 (src/libFLAC/stream_decoder.c and
bitreader.c, and the restore functions of fixed.c and lpc.c), by Josh
Coalson and the Xiph.Org Foundation, made so that damaged FLAC files are
decoded, resynchronized and reported exactly as by the C library, which
uses libFLAC. These translations are in python/src/wfdbx/_flac.py,
cpp/src/flac.cpp, cpp/src/flac.hpp, rust/src/flac.rs, julia/src/flac.jl,
r/R/flac.R, matlab/+wfdbx/+internal/flac_decoder.m and
kotlin/src/commonMain/kotlin/wfdbx/Flac.kt (in the packages, the files
built from them); each carries libFLAC's notice. The FLAC encoders are
WFDB-x's own code. libFLAC itself is not included in WFDB-x, which needs no
external library at run time.

